  "summary": "Git-backed workers each get their own branch and worktree, while Scratch workers get AO-managed branchless directories, to keep parallel work isolated. A project orchestrator agent handles planning and delegation: it breaks plans into tasks, spawns or redirects workers, passes context, and tracks progress, while workers own implementation and PRs.",
